---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Pricing — Thriai" description="Published pricing for Thriai fractional CFO retainers, AI finance platform builds, and revenue systems projects. Fixed project fees and monthly retainers, with requested overflow billed separately.">
  <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom:40px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Pricing</div>
      <h1>Published, fixed, and boring on purpose.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Know the range before the first conversation. Retainers are month to month with thirty days notice. Projects are fixed fee with a defined scope. We do not bill hourly except for overflow work you ask for.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Line 1</div>
      <h2>Fractional CFO retainers</h2>
      <div class="grid c3" style="margin-top:26px">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Foundation</h3>
          <div class="price">$3,500 to $5,000 <small>/ month</small></div>
          <p class="muted">Full-stack startup finance for companies that need investor-ready basics without a hire.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Finance operations oversight with bookkeeping run inside the QA-gated pipeline</li>
            <li>Monthly close and reporting pack</li>
            <li>Cash runway and burn tracking</li>
            <li>Investor and board basics</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="tag hot">Operate</span>
          <h3>Operate</h3>
          <div class="price">$6,000 to $9,000 <small>/ month</small></div>
          <p class="muted">Everything in Foundation, plus an owned close and the reporting a board actually reads.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Owned close with a business-day-5 SLA</li>
            <li>13-week cash forecast</li>
            <li>Budget and budget-vs-actual</li>
            <li>Board package, ARR and KPI marts</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Strategic</h3>
          <div class="price">$10,000 to $15,000 <small>/ month</small></div>
          <p class="muted">Everything in Operate, plus the full CFO motion.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Rolling forecast and scenario modeling</li>
            <li>Fundraise and diligence support</li>
            <li>Pricing and compensation design</li>
            <li>Board and investor work</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:22px">Projects alongside a retainer: Fundraise-Ready package $15K to $35K · M&amp;A and diligence prep $15K to $50K · Financial model build $10K to $35K.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Line 2</div>
      <h2>AI Finance Platform</h2>
      <table style="margin-top:22px">
        <thead><tr><th>Offer</th><th>What you get</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Finance AI Assessment</td><td><b>Two to three weeks.</b> Map the finance stack, quantify automation and agent opportunities, identify governance gaps, deliver a roadmap with ROI.</td><td><b>$8K to $15K</b> fixed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Governed Finance Platform</td><td><b>Six to ten weeks.</b> Governed warehouse, ARR and KPI semantic layer, automated reporting, AI access with guardrails. A foundation built for your finance function.</td><td><b>$25K to $75K</b> fixed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Agent workflow builds</td><td>Close prep, reporting assembly, collections drafts, flux commentary. Each one scoped and tested against the governed model.</td><td><b>$15K to $50K</b> each, plus $1.5K to $3K/mo maintenance</td></tr>
          <tr><td>AI-Native CFO bundle</td><td><b>The flagship.</b> Strategic tier plus the platform plus agents, run as one engagement.</td><td><b>$12K to $20K</b> / month</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Workshops</td><td>Half-day sessions for finance teams and partner firms on AI-native finance operations.</td><td><b>$5K to $10K</b></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Line 3</div>
      <h2>Revenue Systems</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="max-width:64ch">Quote-to-cash integrity, CRM and CPQ architecture, and GTM data that reconciles to the general ledger. Offered to companies where a CFO relationship is the plausible next step.</p>
      <table style="margin-top:22px">
        <thead><tr><th>Offer</th><th>What you get</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Quote-to-Cash Assessment</td><td>Approval leakage, pricing integrity, SKU and discount hygiene, automation risk. Findings quantified in dollars.</td><td><b>$15K to $25K</b> fixed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>ARR Data Quality Rebuild</td><td>CRM to billing to GL entity resolution, bookings classification policy, churn and renewal tracking that ties.</td><td><b>$15K to $40K</b> fixed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>BI Stack Build</td><td>ELT, modeled marts, dashboards, and tie-out tests that check dashboard figures against the ledger.</td><td><b>$25K to $60K</b> fixed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>RevOps retainer</td><td>Ongoing ownership of quote-to-cash systems and GTM data for existing clients.</td><td><b>$3K to $6K</b> / month</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Fine print, in plain language</h2>
      <div class="faq" style="max-width:76ch">
        <details><summary>Why ranges instead of one number?</summary><p>Scope varies with entity count, transaction volume, and how clean the books are on day one. You will get a single fixed number after a 30-minute call, and it will land inside the range shown.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What is not included?</summary><p>Tax return preparation, audits, reviews, and any attest work. We refer those to partner CPA firms and coordinate with them. Payroll processing and transaction-level bookkeeping run through vetted partners inside our quality pipeline and are priced into the retainer.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How does termination work?</summary><p>Retainers are month to month with thirty days written notice. Fixed-fee projects survive termination until delivered unless cancelled individually. Deliverables, models, and the platform repo transfer to you on payment.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do you discount?</summary><p>Founding projects, yes, in exchange for a case study and introductions. Retainer rates, no.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do you carry insurance?</summary><p>Professional liability coverage is bound before the first engagement and liability is capped at fees paid, per the master services agreement.</p></details>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:28px"><a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Get a fixed number</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
